cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you refer to this work, please cite the repository and consult the
  evidence-boundary statement in README.md. No license has been chosen yet;
  contact the author before redistributing.
title: >-
  Photonic Reservoir Computing with a Coherent Optical Delay Line and
  Square-Law Readout
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Kılınç"
    given-names: "Hasan"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hasanklnc011-alt/spiral-delay-reservoir"
date-released: "2026-09-09"
keywords:
  - photonic reservoir computing
  - coherent optical delay
  - square-law photodetection
  - NARMA-10
  - blind evaluation
  - integrated photonics
  - FDTD component validation
abstract: >-
  A staged, blind-tested study of an integrated-photonic architecture that
  generates temporal nonlinear features for the NARMA-10 benchmark using
  coherent time-delayed optical fields and square-law photodetection with a
  trained linear readout. A locked one-shot blind evaluation reaches median
  test NMSE 0.0387 (8/10 seeds below 0.05), beating same-memory linear and
  memory-free controls. A component-level electromagnetic validation campaign
  for the selected architecture is included; its current verdict is
  NOT_PHYSICALLY_ACCEPTED (5 of 11 gates pass). The result is a physically
  parameterized system simulation, not a fabricated device.
